<div class="info">
	<p>
		This is my personal website. The site works like a desktop: click an icon
		to open a window, and press
		<span class="key-close" role="img" aria-label="close button">
			<svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true">
				<path d="M2 2 L8 8 M8 2 L2 8"></path>
			</svg>
		</span>
		or <kbd>esc</kbd> to close them.
	</p>
	<p>Whatever you do, do not press the shutdown button in the taskbar.</p>
	<p>
		This site was created by myself along with Claude.ai. Design is mostly my own, writing is fully mine (yes I use em dashes sometimes), and the code is mostly Claude's.
		Heavily inspired by <a href="https://www.behance.net/gallery/229665053/Web-Portfolio-2" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">this site</a>.
	</p>
</div>

<style>
	.info {
		padding: 24px 28px;
		color: var(--ink);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
	}

	.info p {
		margin: 0 0 14px;
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.info p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	kbd {
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', 'Cascadia Code', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
		font-size: 12px;
		background: rgba(58, 58, 58, 0.1);
		border: 1px solid rgba(58, 58, 58, 0.2);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 1px 5px;
	}

	/* Inline mini close-button, matching the real window control */
	.key-close {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		/* center on the text line, with breathing room either side */
		vertical-align: middle;
		position: relative;
		top: -1px;
		width: 18px;
		height: 18px;
		margin: 0 3px;

		background: var(--close-red);
		border: 2px solid #fff;
		border-radius: 3px;
	}

	.key-close svg {
		width: 8px;
		height: 8px;
		display: block;
	}

	.key-close svg path {
		stroke: #fff;
		stroke-width: 2;
		stroke-linecap: round;
	}
</style>
